+# Findings, ranked
+
+## ISSUE #1 — ACCEPTANCE_GAP (PASS 3) · **blocks DONE**
+
+**Acceptance criterion 2 fails 2 of its 4 cases. Neither new routing path — the §A2 demotion nor
+the §A3 SCOPED+ flavor — can fire on any file in this repository's own `scripts/**` or `hooks/**`.**
+
+### What I ran
+
+The real checkout has an active run (`spec-review` pending), and the hook's fire-condition 7 makes
+it deliberately silent mid-pipeline — so driving it here would have proved nothing. I built a
+sandbox from `git ls-files` (byte-identical tracked content, fresh `git init`, no execution
+directory, empty pre-eval directory) and drove `hooks/triage-prompt-nudge.sh` with synthetic
+`UserPromptSubmit` stdin, one throwaway session id per case.
+
+| # | Request | AC demands | Actual | |
+|---|---|---|---|---|
+| 1 | small edit to `scripts/compound-v-scorecard.py` | `TIER SCOPED` | **`TIER FULL`** (`FULL_PIPELINE`, `override_fired: null`, **no `t3_demotion` key at all**) | ❌ |
+| 2 | small edit to `scripts/compound-v-scope-check.py` | `TIER SCOPED`, `flavor: scoped_plus` | **`TIER FULL`** (`override_fired: 2`, `flavor: null`) | ❌ |
+| 3 | an edit naming a `.env` file | `TIER FULL` | `TIER FULL` | ✅ (but see the note below) |
+| 4 | a `README.md` typo | `TIER DIRECT` | `TIER DIRECT` (`FASTPATH_ELIGIBLE`) | ✅ |
+
+All four records are **schema-valid** against `schemas/pre-eval-record.schema.json` (validated with
+`jsonschema`), so the criterion's second half holds for every case. It is the tiers that are wrong.
+
+### Root cause — one configuration line, not a code defect
+
+Both new routes are gated on the same predicate:
+
+- `scripts/compound-v-preeval.py:565` — `scoped_plus_open = … and not _content_raises_impact(flags)`
+- `scripts/compound-v-preeval.py:644` — `t1_from_broad_glob = … and not content_impact_high`
+
+`_content_raises_impact` (`compound-v-preeval.py:428-435`) returns True on **any** `content:*` flag.
+Those flags come from scanning the **file's own content** against `content_patterns`, and
+`.claude/compound-v-impact-taxonomy.yaml:66-71` carries:
+
+```yaml
+  - match: '%[sd]'
+    pattern_type: regex
+    kind: i18n_placeholder
+    impact_band: high
+```
+
+`%s` / `%d` is ordinary Python string formatting. `scripts/compound-v-scope-check.py` contains 12
+of them (`:277`, `:283`, `:291`, …); `scripts/compound-v-scorecard.py` contains 4. Decision 2's fix
+— `content_scan_exclude` (`.claude/compound-v-impact-taxonomy.yaml:160-161`) — is set to
+`["**/*.md"]` only, so it never reaches code.
+
+The blast radius is not two files. Counted on the merged tree:
+
+> **42 of the 44 files under `scripts/*.py` + `hooks/*.sh` match at least one content pattern**
+> (`%s`/`%d`, or the literal `timeout` — which alone hits 28 of them, `rate_limit`, `price`,
+> `isEnabled`, `consent`).
+
+Every one of those is pinned to `FULL` regardless of how small the change is. That is the exact
+defect decision 1 and decision 3 were written to remove, relocated from the taxonomy's path globs
+into its content patterns.
+
+The taxonomy row itself is not the problem — I checked, and it is correctly broad:
+
+```
+scripts/compound-v-scorecard.py  -> sensitive=False diff=high impact=high  row glob='scripts/**' broad=True
+scripts/compound-v-scope-check.py-> sensitive=True  diff=high impact=high  row glob='scripts/**' broad=True
+```
+
+`broad=True` on both. The demotion had everything it needed except a content scan that did not
+veto it.
+
+### Counterfactual — the engine code is correct
+
+To separate a configuration defect from a code defect I changed **one thing** in the sandbox:
+appended `"**/*.py"` and `"**/*.sh"` to `content_scan_exclude`. Nothing else. Same hook, same
+engine, same requests, fresh pre-eval directory:
+
+```
+LOG: the request needs T3 (reason=demotion) — running the headless classify
+LOG: headless T3 classify: plumbing (backend=claude)
+CTX: TIER: SCOPED (decision SCOPED_PIPELINE …)
+     t3_demotion={"applied": true, "category": "plumbing", "from": {"difficulty":"high","impact":"high"}}
+
+LOG: the request needs T3 (reason=sensitive) — running the headless classify
+LOG: headless T3 classify: plumbing (backend=claude)
+CTX: TIER: SCOPED … SCOPED+ — a small edit on a sensitive path …
+     flavor=scoped_plus
+     t3_demotion={"applied": true, "category":"plumbing", …, "sensitive": true}
+```
+
+Exactly the two outcomes criterion 2 demands. So:
+
+- **The §A2 demotion works.** `t3_reason: "demotion"`, bands capped to `(medium, medium)`, record
+  carries `t3_demotion` with `applied: true`.
+- **The §A3 SCOPED+ flavor works.** `t3_reason: "sensitive"`, `flavor: scoped_plus`,
+  `override_fired: null`, `t3_demotion.sensitive: true`.
+- **Finding 50's headless T3 works live.** `backend=claude` — the nested one-shot ran, answered
+  `plumbing`, and the re-entry with `--t3-category` re-scored cleanly. This is the first evidence in
+  this run that the whole 3.4.1 T3 chain executes end to end, and it does.
+
+Five feature jobs built the mechanism correctly. The configuration the same spec prescribed
+(plan step 4: `content_scan_exclude: ["**/*.md"]`) does not let any of it run here.
+
+→ **Fix at the taxonomy, not at the engine.** The narrow correction is to stop scanning source
+files for prose-shaped patterns — widen `content_scan_exclude`, or make `%[sd]`/`timeout` scoped to
+the file types where they mean what the pattern thinks they mean. Do **not** relax
+`_content_raises_impact`: it is the fail-closed guard, and weakening a check to make a case pass is
+precisely the §2.5 pattern. Then re-run the four-case probe as the acceptance evidence.
+
+### Note on case 3 — it passes, but vacuously
+
+`.env` reached `FULL` through **override #1** (ambiguous localization: the localizer resolved the
+token `.env` to **25 unrelated files** whose text merely contains the string), not through
+`sensitive_path_list` and not through `NEVER_DEMOTE_GLOBS`. The repository has no `.env` file, so
+the hard never-demote list the criterion is really about was never exercised by its own test case.
+The tier is right; the criterion does not prove what it was written to prove. Worth a case that
+actually names an existing secret-shaped path.
