+## ISSUE #2 — INTEGRATION_MISMATCH (PASS 3)
+
+**Three documents still instruct the operator to hand-write `phase: MERGED`, which `/v:dispatch`
+step 9 and the shipped finalizer both now forbid.**
+
+Acceptance criterion 6 names `/v:dispatch` step 9 specifically, and that one is correct —
+`commands/v-dispatch.md:232`:
+
+> **Do not write `phase: MERGED` into `state.json` by hand** — the workflow finalizer has advanced
+> the phase itself since stage 1 (`fix(finalize)`, commit f0dfc30) …
+
+So **criterion 6 passes as written**. But the instruction it repealed still stands, verbatim, in
+three places the pipeline actually reads:
+
+| File:line | Text |
+|---|---|
+| `agents/parallel-dispatcher.md:449` | "**Write `state.json`'s phase as `MERGED` FIRST**, then stage and commit it together with the rest" (Step 7's heading at `:446` is literally "Advance to `MERGED`") |
+| `agents/parallel-dispatcher.md:349` | "Advance `phase` to `MERGED`, commit `state.json` + the run dir …" |
+| `commands/v-resume.md:53` | "On reaching `MERGED` … `state.json` (phase written as `MERGED` first, then committed together with the rest)" |
+| `commands/v-collect.md:114` | "Commit `state.json` (phase `MERGED`) together with the run substrate" |
+
+`agents/parallel-dispatcher.md` is the agent the dispatch path loads. An agent following it does
+the thing `/v:dispatch` step 9 calls "at best a duplicate and at worst a regression of what the
+finalizer recorded" — and the run that produced this very review is a dispatcher run.
+
+This is the same class of defect the 3.4.1 CHANGELOG describes two entries above it ("the phase
+advance to MERGED was a prose step"): the mechanism moved, and only one of the four documents
+that describe it moved with it. It is out of the release job's lane, so it is not that job's
+miss — it is the run's.
+
+→ Bring all four documents onto the finalizer's story: read the phase back, never author it.
