+## ISSUE #4 — QUALITY, low (PASS 3, contract wording)
+
+`results/release.json` reports `tests.scope: "impacted"` on a job whose manifest `triage.tier` is
+`FULL`. `agents/spec-reviewer.md` §3.3 says the resolved scope "must match what the tier owes", and
+FULL owes `full`. Read literally, a correct FULL run trips its own reviewer contract.
+
+It is a label, not a gap: `jobs/release.test-contract.json` carries `full_command` verbatim in
+`resolved_commands`, it ran, and it exited 0. I reproduced the labelling directly — at
+`triage.tier: FULL` with an unmapped changed path, `resolve-tests` emits `"scope": "impacted"`
+while resolving floor + `full_command`, because `scope` reports the job's declared/derived slice
+and the tier's escalation is applied on top of it.
+
+→ Either the resolver should promote the label to `full` when it adds `full_command`, or §3.3
+should say that `scope` reports the declared slice and the tier obligation is checked against
+`resolved_commands`. As it stands the two documents disagree, and the next reviewer will either
+raise a false BUILD_RED or learn to ignore the field.
+
